==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|hight||tr=alternative past participle of {{term|hoten|lang=enm}}|to be named, be called|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|heht|hēht|tr=preterite of {{term|hatan|hātan|lang=ang}}|to be named, be called|lang=ang}}, from *''hehait-'', reduplicate preterite base of {{proto|Germanic|haitanan|to call, command, summon|lang=en}}, from {{proto|Indo-European|key(w)-||kyew-|to set in motion|lang=en}}. Cognate with {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|heißen|lang=de}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|hedde|lang=da}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|heten|lang=nl}}, and {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|heta|lang=sv}}, {{la}} {{term|cieo|cieō|I call, I set in motion|lang=la}}. More at {{l|en|citation}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/haɪt/}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|hights|highting|hight}}
# {{archaic|transitive}} To [[call]], [[name]].
# {{archaic|intransitive}} To be called or named.

